<Layout title="Drylining Musselburgh | Partition Walls &amp; Ceilings Contractors" description="Professional drylining contractors in Musselburgh. Expert partition walls, suspended ceilings, and plasterboard installation for Musselburgh, East Lothian, and the wider EH21 postcode region. Free quotes." canonical="/areas/musselburgh/" schema={schema}>
  <section style="position:relative;min-height:400px;display:flex;align-items:center;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#1a1a2e 0%,#16213e 100%);overflow:hidden;"> <img src="/images/hero-main.jpg" alt="Drylining services in Musselburgh and East Lothian" style="position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;opacity:0.25;"> <div class="container" style="position:relative;z-index:1;text-align:center;padding:60px 20px;"> <nav style="font-size:13px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.70);margin-bottom:12px;"> <a href="/" style="text-decoration:none;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.70);">Home</a> / <a href="/areas/" style="text-decoration:none;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.70);">Areas</a> / <span style="color:#ffffff;">Drylining in Musselburgh</span> </nav> <h1 style="font-size:clamp(28px,4vw,44px);font-weight:800;color:#ffffff;margin-bottom:14px;line-height:1.15;">Drylining in Musselburgh</h1> <p style="font-size:17px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.85);max-width:700px;margin:0 auto;line-height:1.6;">CSCS-accredited drylining contractors delivering partition walls, suspended ceilings, and plasterboard across Musselburgh, East Lothian, and the wider EH21 postcode region.</p> </div> </section> <section class="section"><div class="container" style="max-width:900px;"> <div style="padding:24px;margin-bottom:24px;border-left:4px solid var(--primary);background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);"> <p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;color:var(--text);"><strong>TL;DR:</strong> Drylining Musselburgh provides drylining, partition walls, and suspended ceilings across Musselburgh (EH21), East Lothian, and the wider area. Experienced with historic burgh properties, new residential developments, and commercial fit-outs.</p> </div> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Drylining Services in Musselburgh</h2> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Musselburgh is Scotland's oldest burgh, situated on the south bank of the Firth of Forth approximately 5 miles east of Edinburgh city centre. The EH21 postcode covers the historic town centre, residential suburbs, and the rapidly growing western suburbs where Edinburgh's expansion meets East Lothian. With a population of around 22,000, Musselburgh is a popular commuter town with strong community ties, a vibrant harbour area, and the famous Musselburgh Racecourse. The town has experienced significant residential development in recent years, with new housing estates on the western fringes and ongoing refurbishment of the historic building stock, creating steady demand for quality drylining services across all property types.</p> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Our Musselburgh crew covers the entire EH21 postcode and surrounding East Lothian areas, serving a diverse mix of projects from the carefully listed properties along the High Street to new build housing developments on the town's edges. We bring the same level of Scottish Building Standards expertise to Musselburgh as we do across the wider Edinburgh region, delivering quality drylining, partition walls, and suspended ceilings to residential and commercial clients alike.</p> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">What We Do in Musselburgh</h2> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Our Musselburgh-based crew handles everything from historic burgh property refurbishments to new build pre-completion drylining — covering partition walls, suspended ceilings, and fire-rated wall systems across the EH21 postcode and East Lothian.</p> <ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;"> <li><strong>Historic property drylining</strong> — Internal wall insulation, room conversions, and partition walls in Musselburgh's listed 17th and 18th-century burgh properties</li> <li><strong>New build drylining</strong> — Pre-completion drylining for new residential developments on the western fringes of Musselburgh</li> <li><strong>Commercial fit-outs</strong> — Office refurbs, retail units, and hospitality venues along Musselburgh's High Street and business areas</li> <li><strong>Fire-rated walls</strong> — Multi-storey residential and commercial buildings requiring Scottish Building Standards Section 2 (Fire) compliance</li> <li><strong>Suspended ceilings</strong> — Commercial premises, offices, and new build apartments across East Lothian</li> <li><strong>Acoustic partitions</strong> — Residential properties in new housing estates and refurbishment projects</li> </ul> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Areas of Musselburgh We Cover</h2> <ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;"> <li>Musselburgh town centre and High Street (EH21)</li> <li>The Harbour and Waterfront area</li> <li>East Linton and coastal properties (EH22)</li> <li>Haddington (EH41) — 15 minutes via A698</li> <li>North Berwick (EH39) — 30 minutes via A198</li> <li>Portobello (EH15) — adjacent to Musselburgh</li> <li>Wallyford and Longniddry (EH32)</li> <li>Prestonkirk and Gullane area (EH31)</li> <li>Rest and Fairnone area</li> <li>East Lothian area generally</li> </ul> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Musselburgh Building Regulations &amp; Planning</h2> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Musselburgh falls under <strong>East Lothian Council</strong> for building standards and planning. The town centre contains numerous listed buildings, particularly along the historic High Street and around the Harbour. Properties within conservation areas may require listed building consent for internal structural alterations. We work closely with clients, architects, and the council's building standards department to ensure every project — from a historic property internal refurbishment to a new build commercial fit-out — is fully compliant with Scottish Building Standards and any local conservation requirements.</p> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Why Choose Us for Musselburgh Projects</h2> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">As an Edinburgh-based drylining team, we have extensive experience working across East Lothian, including Musselburgh, Haddington, and North Berwick. We understand the unique character of Musselburgh — from its rich history as Scotland's oldest burgh to its position as one of Edinburgh's most desirable commuter towns. Our crew is familiar with Scottish Building Standards and the particular requirements of working in a historic East Lothian burgh. Whether you need drylining for a historic property conversion, a new build project, or a commercial refurbishment, our team delivers quality work on time.</p> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Related Services</h2> <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(180px,1fr));gap:10px;margin-bottom:1.5rem;"> <a href="/services/partition-walls/" style="text-decoration:none;padding:10px 14px;background:var(--white);border-radius:6px;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;border:1px solid var(--border);color:var(--text);">Partition Walls</a> <a href="/services/fire-rated-drylining/" style="text-decoration:none;padding:10px 14px;background:var(--white);border-radius:6px;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;border:1px solid var(--border);color:var(--text);">Fire-Rated Drylining</a> <a href="/services/acoustic-drylining/" style="text-decoration:none;padding:10px 14px;background:var(--white);border-radius:6px;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;border:1px solid var(--border);color:var(--text);">Acoustic Drylining</a> <a href="/services/refurbishment-drylining/" style="text-decoration:none;padding:10px 14px;background:var(--white);border-radius:6px;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;border:1px solid var(--border);color:var(--text);">Refurbishment Drylining</a> </div> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Nearby Areas</h2> <ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;"> <li><a href="/areas/edinburgh/" style="color:var(--primary);text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;">Edinburgh</a> — 15 minutes via A1</li> <li><a href="/areas/dalkeith/" style="color:var(--primary);text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;">Dalkeith</a> — 20 minutes via A702</li> <li><a href="/areas/haddington/" style="color:var(--primary);text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;">Haddington</a> — 15 minutes via A698</li> <li><a href="/areas/livingston/" style="color:var(--primary);text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;">Livingston</a> — 35 minutes via M8</li> </ul> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Get a Free Musselburgh Quote</h2> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:2rem;">We offer free, no-obligation site visits and written quotes for all drylining projects across Musselburgh. Call us or fill in our quick form.</p> <div style="margin-top:2rem;text-align:center;"> <a href="/get-quote/" class="btn btn-primary" style="font-size:1.0625rem;padding:1rem 2.5rem;">Get a Free Musselburgh Quote</a> <a href="tel:08008203090" class="btn btn-secondary" style="font-size:1.0625rem;padding:1rem 2.5rem;border:2px solid var(--primary);background:transparent;color:var(--primary);margin-left:0.5rem;">FREEPHONE 0800 820 3090</a> </div> </div></section>  
